#X obj 723 8 z~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 240 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Delays the input audio signal by an integer number of
samples. The delay length is set by the argument or by the @z property
and can be changed at run time through the control inlet.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 178 • Sample-accurate alignment — compensating small timing
offsets between two signals (for example \, between a dry and a delayed
path) \, with exact sample precision rather than millisecond resolution.;
#X text 250 248 • Building feedback paths and comb filters — creating
short comb-filter effects \, Karplus-Strong strings or feedback delays
by combining [z~] with a feedback loop.;
